WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:09.749
This video shows how the web player tells your code what happens. It reports when an animation finishes, and every problem it meets, so the page can react.

2
00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:14.969
Let's start with an intro animation, and show the welcome section when it finishes.

3
00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:39.063
When the intro finishes, the on finish callback shows the welcome section. The animation decides when.

4
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:47.405
Problems arrive the same way, through callbacks. First, a small function that lists each problem on the page.

5
00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:04.768
Each problem has a code, and a kind that says who can fix it.

6
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:13.497
Now two more players, both reporting to that function. One file has a broken effect, and the other file is missing.

7
00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:42.814
The broken effect is a warning, so that ball still plays. The missing file is an error, so nothing plays there. Each one shows its code and kind, the document or the host page.

8
00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:53.777
So, the player tells your code when it finishes, and reports every problem with a code and a kind. Handle them in your code, and the console stays quiet.
